ts above its blended-model fair value of $11.72 (margin of safety -279%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 13%).","On multiples it looks cheap against Industrials peers: EV/EBITDA 9.3 vs 13.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 354% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -3.8% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 1.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 24 covering analysts target $49.89 on average, 12% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 4% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.7%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.43).","It burns cash (FCF margin -3%).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 4.18x.","ROE of 6% is amplified by 3.6x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.4% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.7x net debt to EBITDA ($3.2B of cash against $4.6B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.6x.","The current ratio of 0.52 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.6% over 3 years, 25.4% over 5 years and 3.5% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 27%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 13%.","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (9.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 22, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.0%, and institutions hold 95%.","It returns 13.6% a year to shareholders (11.7% in buybacks and 1.6% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."